in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/spectral

# @mirror/spectral/observation — the 16-feature input layer Fate sees.
#
# Recognition #58 v1 closure (per
# [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]]): Fate inference IS a
# 5-layer D²NN + Fabry-Perot resonator + Reck/Clements unitary mesh.
# The recognition was promoted 2026-06-11; v1 closure was pending the
# substrate declaration of *what the input dimension carries*. The
# 5-layer D²NN's input layer is 16-dimensional; until this shard
# lands, the 16 features are implicit (named in
# `docs/specs/spectral-db-mirror.md §3.2`, but never declared at
# substrate altitude).
#
# This shard closes that gap. It declares the 16 graph-observation
# features as one typed carrier under `@mirror/spectral` (form-side
# family, per recognition #55: form-side species observe; process-side
# species transform). The observation IS the family's read surface
# for Fate's inference altitude.
#
# === The recognition: the family root already named this ===
#
# `shards/mirror/spectral.mirror` (the family root) declares
# `@mirror/spectral` as the orchestra's OBSERVATION surface. The
# 16-feature graph_observation IS the substrate-altitude form of that
# observation — what the Fabry-Perot resonator's gain media (per
# `shards/optics/source/ganglion/*`) actually read at the input layer.
#
# The family-root sub-shard list already implies it (the score reads
# eigenboard + metalogue + pending; the observation reads the
# substrate's *current geometry*). Score and observation are sibling
# form-side species: score is the orchestra's shared-state read
# surface; observation is the input-layer read surface that drives
# the audition's 5-layer D²NN.
#
# === The 16 features ===
#
# Verbatim from `docs/specs/spectral-db-mirror.md §3.2`. Each feature
# is a unit-interval scalar (`f64 ∈ [0,1]`). The 16 names partition
# into four conceptual quadrants of four each:
#
#   Settlement-state (what the substrate is right now):
#     convergence_settled    is the spectral loop converged?
#     pressure_load          how much pending work is queued?
#     node_occupancy         how full is the graph's node capacity?
#     edge_density           how richly connected is the graph?
#
#   Crystal-state (where the substrate is along its crystallization):
#     crystal_fraction       fraction of nodes that have crystallized
#     settlement_depth       depth into the kintsugi-oscillation
#     interval_ratio         oscillation interval / reference interval
#     hot_path_density       fraction of paths in hot-path band
#
#   Query-state (what the substrate is being asked):
#     query_intensity        rate of incoming queries
#     partition_risk         probability of partition under current load
#     tick_maturity          fraction of expected tick duration consumed
#     mutation_rate          rate of structural mutations
#
#   Spectral-state (what the eigenvalues are doing):
#     shannon_loss_rate      Shannon entropy loss per tick
#     spectral_dimension     effective dimension of the spectral manifold
#     eigenvalue_gap         λ₁ − λ₀ of the graph Laplacian
#     holonomy               closure defect of the oscillation round
#
# These four quadrants ARE the 5×5 conductivity tensor's four
# eigen-axes after dropping λ₀ (the dark / generative-zero
# eigenvalue). The 16 = 4 axes × 4 features per axis is the
# substrate-pull alignment with the @hash/coincidence geometry; not
# coincidence, identity (per recognition #58's D²NN witness chain).
#
# === Type discipline ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: no bare `f64`. Each feature is
# `unit_interval` — the substrate's typed `[0,1]` carrier. The
# refinement (`0 ≤ x ≤ 1`) belongs at @epistemologic/property altitude
# (`@epistemologic/property/unit_interval`); this shard declares the
# *type* and forward-references the property predicate as the
# verification surface.
#
# `unit_interval` is declared here as a sub-shard-local newtype on
# first use; if a sibling shard surfaces the same need (the
# substrate-already-had-the-word pattern), the lift to a shared
# carrier is a future cascade tick, not this one's burden. The 22nd-
# instance flag from `score.mirror`'s landing is the right precedent
# (sibling shards lift carriers; the family root doesn't pre-declare
# them).
#
# === Forward-promise to consumers ===
#
# This shard declares the carrier. The substrate-altitude consumers
# (the action that *fills* `graph_observation` from a `score`; the
# action that *feeds* `graph_observation` into the audition's
# Fabry-Perot input layer) land downstream as the recognition #58
# cascade reaches its consumers. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]:
# this is the carrier landing; the morphism that fills it is the
# next tick when the consumer pulls.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-db-mirror.md §3.2 (the 16
#               features verbatim),
#               docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §4.5 (the score sibling),
#               docs/insights/recognition #58 / fate-is-optical-inference
#               (the 5-layer D²NN witness; the input-layer dimension).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]]
#                      (#58; the recognition this shard closes the v1
#                      gap of),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                      (#55; observation IS form-side under @mirror/spectral),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (unit_interval is the
#                      typed carrier; no f64 escapes),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (the 16-feature
#                      vocabulary already existed in the spec; this
#                      shard names it at substrate altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the form-side observation surface was already
#                      implied by the family root; this shard realises
#                      what the root named).
# Related shards: mirror/spectral.mirror (the family root; this shard
#                 is a sibling form-side species to score),
#                 mirror/spectral/score.mirror (the orchestra's
#                 shared-state read surface; observation reads the
#                 substrate geometry at a different altitude),
#                 optics/source/ganglion/*.mirror (the 5 gain media
#                 that consume this observation at the Fabry-Perot
#                 input layer per recognition #58),
#                 hash/coincidence.mirror (the 5×5 conductivity tensor
#                 whose eigen-axes the four observation quadrants
#                 align with).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/spectral/observation.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/spectral/observation` as a species under the
# `@mirror/spectral` family.

prism @mirror/spectral/observation {
  focus observation
  project observation
  split observation
  shift observation
  settle observation
}

# === The unit-interval carrier ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: the typed `[0,1]` scalar. The
# refinement predicate (`0 ≤ x ≤ 1`) is `@epistemologic/property/
# unit_interval` (forward-promised; not declared by this shard).
# Locally a newtype over f64; the property predicate enforces the
# interval on construction.
type unit_interval = f64

# === The 16-feature observation carrier ===
#
# The orchestra's input-layer observation. Recognition #58's 5-layer
# D²NN reads this record's 16 scalars as its input-layer activations.
# Four conceptual quadrants of four features each (per the body
# documentation above); each scalar is a unit_interval refined by
# the @epistemologic/property/unit_interval predicate.
type graph_observation = {
  # Settlement-state quadrant
  convergence_settled:  unit_interval,
  pressure_load:        unit_interval,
  node_occupancy:       unit_interval,
  edge_density:         unit_interval,

  # Crystal-state quadrant
  crystal_fraction:     unit_interval,
  settlement_depth:     unit_interval,
  interval_ratio:       unit_interval,
  hot_path_density:     unit_interval,

  # Query-state quadrant
  query_intensity:      unit_interval,
  partition_risk:       unit_interval,
  tick_maturity:        unit_interval,
  mutation_rate:        unit_interval,

  # Spectral-state quadrant
  shannon_loss_rate:    unit_interval,
  spectral_dimension:   unit_interval,
  eigenvalue_gap:       unit_interval,
  holonomy:             unit_interval,
}

out @mirror/spectral/observation
out unit_interval
out graph_observation
